# Serve these byte for byte.
#
# The app checks a SHA256 from manifest.json before it will use a downloaded list, and
# that hash is computed over the file as it sits on disk. If git normalises line endings
# on the way in or out, the bytes raw.githubusercontent.com serves no longer match the
# hash and the app correctly refuses the update — which looks like "the list never
# updates" and is tedious to trace. Marking them binary keeps the two identical.
*.json -text
*.bin  -text
